      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["R5", "T2"],
      "pins": ["T2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3V3"],
      "observed": "R5 (10 kΩ) connects the +3V3 rail to the gate (pin 1) of T2 (IRLR2905), the low-side N-MOSFET for the main circulation pump; T1's collector also drives this same gate node.",
      "expected": "A low-side N-FET gate should be pulled to GND so the pump is off when the pre-driver is inactive. The equivalent ATO-valve driver uses a base pull-down (R12 10 kΩ) for fail-off behaviour instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "+3V3 power flag -> R5 10k -> gate (pin 1) of T2 IRLR2905, shared with collector of T1 BT3904"}
      ],
      "impact": "T2 is held on by default whenever T1 is off, so the main circulation pump is energised (fail-on) and the control sense is inverted relative to the intended low-side switch.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the intended design: the ATO-valve control is wired to ESP32 IO7 instead of the specified IO2, and the main-pump MOSFET gate carries a +3V3 pull-up (fail-on) rather than a pull-down. Both changes would make the board behave differently from the specified design."
}

